# .github/upstream-compat.env
#
# Which upstream OpenShell gateway the interop smoke tests against.
#
#   latest    Track bleeding edge. This is the default and the intended
#             steady state.
#   vN.N.NN   Pin. Use ONLY when upstream itself is broken and is blocking
#             unrelated pull requests. Revert as soon as upstream is fixed.
#
# `latest` resolves to the newest upstream semver RELEASE TAG, then to an
# immutable digest. It is never the mutable `:latest` container tag — that
# tag moved twice in one week and silently handed every new sandbox an
# unreviewed privileged supervisor binary.
#
# Changing this value is a reviewable commit on purpose: it records that
# upstream was broken during a window, instead of leaving it in someone's
# memory. See docs/internal/runbook-upstream-sync.md.
GATEWAY_REF=v0.0.116

# PIN_REASON and PIN_REVIEW_AFTER only mean something while GATEWAY_REF is
# pinned to a version, not `latest`. They exist because a pin is silent
# once it's in place: while pinned, resolve-upstream-refs.sh resolves only
# the pinned ref, so the weekly drift check has nothing upstream-shaped to
# compare it against and stays green forever. Nothing else notices the pin
# can be lifted, so the reason it went in has to be written down, or it
# won't be reconstructable months later. scripts/check-pin-status.sh reads
# both of these to report whether the pin still holds.
#
#   PIN_REASON        Why upstream is broken and this pin exists. Free text.
#   PIN_REVIEW_AFTER   YYYY-MM-DD. A date past which the pin is worth a
#                      second look, not a hard deadline.
#
# Fill both in in the same commit that sets GATEWAY_REF to a version --
# a pin recorded without its reason is how the reason gets lost.
PIN_REASON=Upstream v0.1.2 is a minor-version bump that moved the gateway's whole configuration surface. At least four separate breaking changes, found one CI cycle at a time: (1) inference.local and the managed inference router removed (architectural -- see scripts/check-inference-local.sh); (2) --drivers replaced by a singular --compute-driver; (3) the gateway config must now be a regular file, not a ConfigMap symlink; (4) the config schema itself rewritten -- of the six fields this chart emits, only log_level is still valid at top level. (2) and (3) are already fixed version-compatibly. This pin buys time to do (1) and (4) as deliberate work rather than discovering breakages one 10-minute CI run at a time, and it unblocks unrelated PRs meanwhile. Lift it as soon as the migration tests green against v0.1.x.
PIN_REVIEW_AFTER=2026-10-31

# Set when the pin is NOT waiting on artifact availability.
#
# check-pin-status.sh answers one question: "do images and a CLI exist for a
# newer tag?" That is the right question for a pin held because upstream
# tagged without publishing. It is the WRONG question for a pin held because
# a newer release needs migration work -- there the artifacts exist, so the
# script would report the reason evaporated and advise unpinning straight
# back into the breakage.
#
# Any non-empty value suppresses the evaporation verdict and is echoed in the
# weekly report instead. Clear it when the blocking work is done.
PIN_BLOCKED_BY=v0.1.2 migration: gateway config schema + inference.local removal
